01:16:43.520 --> 01:16:49.820
So, like, it was a nice bite-sized thing, and I think that for what they set out to do, I think it works really well.

01:16:49.900 --> 01:16:53.920
And I really appreciate, like, the balance it brings to it.

01:16:53.940 --> 01:16:55.480
It's a decent amount of strategy.

01:16:55.640 --> 01:16:57.700
It doesn't get, like, it never goes overboard.

01:16:58.100 --> 01:17:03.760
Not overboard, but it never gets too robust, which is fine for a bite-sized thing like this.

01:17:03.880 --> 01:17:05.820
But I'll say this.

01:17:05.820 --> 01:17:07.100
I feel like I'm not really saying anything.

01:17:07.100 --> 01:17:16.740
So I'll say that, like, this is a game that, like, I did at one point consider putting it on the Essential Games, which I feel like is saying something.

01:17:17.220 --> 01:17:29.520
But what keeps it off for me is just the fact that, I mean, for one, that, like, some of the minigames, you know, like, don't feel like they kind of feed into the overall vision as well.

01:17:29.520 --> 01:17:39.240
And they, you know, while some of them might be fun on their own and others not, like, they all don't, like, it's not cohesive in, like, this strategy game always.

01:17:40.200 --> 01:17:44.880
Although, you know, here to contradict myself again, sometimes I think that they actually do work pretty well.

01:17:44.940 --> 01:17:47.340
And I do appreciate that they, like, mix it up.

01:17:47.440 --> 01:17:55.800
But the bigger thing that keeps it off for me is just the knowledge that there are so many other versions of this game and, like, how popular it is.

01:17:55.800 --> 01:18:07.620
And I know we don't like to do that too much, but, like, I just feel like if Defender of the Crown is essential, it's not this original, well, not original, but this early NES version of Defender of the Crown.

01:18:07.740 --> 01:18:12.540
Like, I'm sure that they've done, you know, they've done it better going forward.

01:18:12.540 --> 01:18:20.500
And I've even played other NES games that have, like, this kind of element, which I alluded to earlier, that I think have done it better.

01:18:20.500 --> 01:18:37.740
So, like, as impressed as I was with this, where we are right now in, you know, in 1989, when I step back and look at it from my 2021 perspective, I feel like it's not enough.

01:18:37.980 --> 01:18:39.020
So I'm going to say no.

01:18:39.400 --> 01:18:42.920
