01:18:52.820 --> 01:18:58.040
And that is, this game is overall, like, you know, a good time.

01:18:58.620 --> 01:19:02.080
You know, maybe that gives away too much already on my vote, but, like, it's overall a good time.

01:19:02.840 --> 01:19:06.180
The game wants you to think that you can do a lot of things.

01:19:06.820 --> 01:19:14.920
And you can. Like, we talked about a lot of different minigames that are included, the defensive sieges, the jousting, right?

01:19:15.540 --> 01:19:20.100
But a lot of that stuff, you know, you could choose to pursue it.

01:19:20.240 --> 01:19:21.400
You don't have to.

01:19:21.600 --> 01:19:22.660
It's not necessary.

01:19:22.980 --> 01:19:32.440
The game really is all about acquiring gold fast, building an army fast, acquiring land fast, doing this fast.

01:19:32.440 --> 01:19:42.180
The faster you play through this game, and I found this through trial and error, is that, like, the longer you let this game go on, the chances of failure just continue to occur.

01:19:42.380 --> 01:19:53.440
I really feel like this game, rather than being an open-ended strategy game where the choices are yours, it's actually just pushing you in one particular direction to do certain things.

01:19:53.460 --> 01:19:58.880
I can't think of an actual reason unless you pick the wrong starting character.

01:19:58.880 --> 01:20:01.520
And I'm not saying, like, there's an objectively good one.

01:20:01.600 --> 01:20:03.900
I'm just saying, like, the wrong starting character that would require this to happen.

01:20:04.100 --> 01:20:06.640
I can't think of a good reason to call a tournament.

01:20:07.440 --> 01:20:09.760
There's better uses of your turn.

01:20:09.980 --> 01:20:11.520
There's better uses of your gold.

01:20:11.920 --> 01:20:19.520
The game wants you to think that, you know, you have all this freedom and ability similar to a game like Nobunaga's Ambition.

01:20:19.520 --> 01:20:25.580
But you don't really have that if you want any chance at winning this game or doing well in this game.

01:20:26.080 --> 01:20:37.800
Maybe after, you know, many, many hours of playthrough, you'll find other, not necessarily better strategies, but different strategies so that you can use the other elements of this game.

01:20:37.880 --> 01:20:39.760
But you don't have to ever use those elements.

01:20:39.960 --> 01:20:44.580
And so ultimately this, what I was calling grander strategy, right?

01:20:44.580 --> 01:20:51.020
It's not a modern-day grand strategy game, but it's grander than what we're accustomed to on these types of NES games.

01:20:51.300 --> 01:21:02.080
It's ultimately not that grand at all because it's kind of shoehorning you into a specific set of actions that don't necessarily make me feel like I'm in control.

01:21:02.340 --> 01:21:06.780
It just makes me feel like I'm doing things so that I can continue on winning.

01:21:07.280 --> 01:21:09.760
And that's not fun for me in a strategy game.

01:21:09.860 --> 01:21:13.240
In a strategy game, I much prefer to be the one making those decisions.

01:21:13.240 --> 01:21:25.240
So the ultimate verdict here is that the guiding of the game, the way that the game was balanced and designed, causes me to play this game in a very specific way that I don't want to but feel like I ultimately have to.

01:21:25.400 --> 01:21:28.580
And so therefore for me, this is not an essential game.

